<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss May trade surplus revised up to 366 mln Sfr.</title>
<headline>Swiss May trade surplus revised up to 366 mln Sfr.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Switzerland's trade surplus in May was revised to 366.2 million Swiss francs from a provisional figure of 359.7 million, the Federal Customs Office said.</p>
<p>It gave these revised figures for May:</p>
<p> Balance  (million Sfr)	   366.2</p>
<p> Imports  (million Sfr)	   7,815.5</p>
<p> Exports  (million Sfr)	   8,181.8</p>
<p>Provisional figures had shown imports of 7,814.4 million and exports of 8,174.0 million Swiss francs. These figures exclude trade in precious metals, precious stones, art objects and antiques. -- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
</text>
